Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 09:52:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 117/117] Refresh the shell clock's time-zone cache after a
 zone change

Ported from the Windows guest (0111). The Omarchy clock widget calls
Date.timeZoneUpdated() before redrawing, so a followed host zone shows
without restarting the shell.

Existing disks get the time-zone service through compatibility revision
48 but the widget only through an Omarchy upgrade. The service now
repairs the widget before the display manager starts, replacing it only
when it still has the digest earlier images shipped.
